WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.666
Video ten. A purchase from another state, and
your bills.

00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:09.884
Inside Gujarat, the tax is CGST + SGST.

00:00:09.814 --> 00:00:14.564
From another state, the tax is IGST: one
ledger with the full rate.

00:00:14.864 --> 00:00:17.881
V, then F9: Purchase.

00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:23.398
Type the supplier's invoice number, MF/118,
and its date.

00:00:23.709 --> 00:00:27.459
The party: Mehta Fabrics. Then the Purchase
Account.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.645
Cotton Fabric, into Ring Road Warehouse: 300
metres at 115 rupees.

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:41.678
Click below the item, and select IGST. Hisaab
calculates ₹1,725.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:46.726
Type the narration. Hisaab asks: Accept? Y for
yes.

00:00:48.419 --> 00:00:53.836
The bill-wise details open. The bill is a new
reference: MF/118.

00:00:53.866 --> 00:00:57.683
The credit period of Mehta Fabrics gives 45
days.

00:00:57.713 --> 00:01:01.996
You can type a date in place of the days: 16
May 2026.

00:01:02.026 --> 00:01:04.311
Ctrl+A saves the purchase.

00:01:05.461 --> 00:01:07.746
Esc takes you to the Gateway.

00:01:07.832 --> 00:01:12.115
Alt+G, type "bills pay", and press Enter:
Bills Payable.

00:01:12.814 --> 00:01:19.365
Bill MF/118 of Mehta Fabrics: ₹36,225, due on
16 May.

00:01:19.395 --> 00:01:26.547
Bills Receivable shows the other side: bill 1
of Sharma Traders, ₹53,025, due on 1 May.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:30.860
You get ₹53,025 from your customer.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:35.073
You pay ₹36,225 to your supplier.

00:01:35.274 --> 00:01:39.759
Every bill has a due date. Next: payment,
receipt and contra.

